{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788161286,"nonce":"nyCfFOn/9Y57b0erZnGgonrRBH0=","title":"ci: the coverage ratchet is red on main (77.1% vs a 79.5% floor) and blocks every PR","message":"`ci/coverage` is a **required** check and it fails on `main`, so it currently\nblocks every PR regardless of content.\n\n```\ncoverage ratchet: scarab-executor-local: 77.1% \u003c baseline 80.0% - 0.5pp\n```\n\nBaseline is `scarab-executor-local = 80.0` in `docs/audits/coverage-baseline.toml`\nwith 0.5pp tolerance, so the floor is 79.5%.\n\nNot a PR-local failure — verified by re-reading the ratchet line out of the\n`coverage` job logs on `main` itself:\n\n| commit | run | `scarab-executor-local` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `71408823` | 33171953337 | 79.0% |\n| `731bc427` | 33173297743 | 79.0% |\n| `6bf00bb` | 33271279118 | **77.1%** |\n| `d8e748f4` | 33297280454 | **77.1%** |\n\nSo it slipped under the floor some time ago at 79.0%, and then dropped a further\n1.9pp. Every recent `ci` run on `main` is red, always this same job. PR #3\n(UI/art only, zero Rust) reproduces the message byte-for-byte, which is how it\nwas confirmed to be inherited rather than caused.\n\nThe most recent commit touching that crate is `13de34f feat(server): add the\ninfra observer (ADR-0068)` — the likely source of the second drop, worth\nchecking first.\n\nTwo legitimate fixes and they mean different things:\n\n* **Add tests** to `scarab-executor-local` to get back over 79.5% — right if the\n  ADR-0068 observer paths genuinely want coverage.\n* **Lower the baseline** to reflect reality — right only if that code is\n  deliberately untested, and it should be a deliberate, recorded decision rather\n  than a quiet number change.\n\nWhichever: while `main` is red the ratchet protects nothing and the required-check\ngate is noise, so this wants settling before or alongside the CI-simplification\nwork.","files":null}]}